-- Pipeline row status + notes append for TN Gov R primary.
-- Run ONLY after fixes-2026-08-02.sql is committed.
-- Status moves audited -> published (one step BACK) because the 2026-08-01 audit's
-- "no unresolved high-severity findings" conclusion did not hold: two of the eleven
-- drafts were not verifiable in their cited source. 'published' is the correct
-- lifecycle state for "drafts inserted, audit not yet clean" per race-pipeline
-- SKILL.md, and it puts the race BACK in the work queue -- the queue excludes
-- status in ('audited','skipped','blocked'), so at 'audited' this race was invisible
-- with 0 rankable topics and the primary on 2026-08-06. Not using 'blocked': that
-- would also hide it from the queue.

UPDATE essentials.readrank_race_pipeline SET
  status = 'published',
  status_reason = 'Source-verification pass 2026-08-02 found 2 drafts unverifiable in their cited source (1 a misattribution); fixes applied, needs re-audit + live selection.',
  notes = notes || E'\n---\nSOURCE-VERIFICATION PASS 2026-08-02 (publish-quotes editorial review of all 11 drafts against their cited sources; every quote re-fetched).\nSupersedes the 2026-08-01 "no unresolved high-severity findings" conclusion -- that audit ran mechanical + in-context judgment checks but never re-fetched the source pages, so it could not see the two fidelity failures below.\n\nHIGH (2) -- quote not present in cited source:\n1. Blackburn/deportation 32980122 -- "Let''s make certain our communities are safe... let''s pick up the pace deporting illegal aliens" does NOT appear in the cited WVLT article. Real source is WSMV 2026-07-25, where Blackburn is RELAYING VOTERS: "People will say, ''Hey, let''s make certain our communities are safe, our schools are safe, let''s pick up the pace deporting illegal aliens.''" The draft stripped that framing and presented voters'' words as her own pledge, labelled "Verbatim, no edits". REPLACED (user decision) with a genuine first-person commitment from her own "Can''t Stay" campaign ad (Nashville Banner 2026-07-16): "As governor, I''ll deport illegals, stop the flow of drugs and drug money." Note the tier drop -- paid campaign media, not an interview answer. NB: WVLT''s "Let''s cooperate with ICE," she said is the SAME remark also stripped of its "people are saying" framing by the publisher -- do not reuse it as her position.\n2. Fritts/public-safety-approach 29d84e19 -- also absent from the cited WVLT article; real source WSMV 2026-07-25, and the draft cut the load-bearing closing clause. Restored to "...entire careers in Memphis doing the job of the local law enforcement." and re-cited to WSMV.\n\nMEDIUM (3) -- edits not honestly marked:\n3. Blackburn/taxes 577f9663 -- spoken "big red marker AND programs" had been silently changed to "to". Now bracketed "[to]".\n4. Rose/housing 5da17c8d -- draft ended mid-sentence and used "[and]" for a comma; restored the full verbatim Banner sentence, bracket removed.\n5. Rose/public-safety-approach 8e8928c8 -- draft cut "to confront crime and the willingness to do so"; restored.\n\nRESOLVED from the 2026-08-01 audit: 2 of the 3 non-differentiating-goal mediums are fixed by restoring the cut clauses -- Fritts public-safety (29d84e19) now names the mechanism (Guard should not substitute for local police) and Rose public-safety (8e8928c8) now carries the contestable "willingness" claim. Both note-too-long lows fixed. Editor notes rewritten on all 11 rows: 4 opened with a dangling "From the same ... interview" and did not stand alone; Fritts/deportation claimed a leading "So" that appears in no printed source; Fritts/vouchers cited a constitutional article he never named; Blackburn/vouchers said "keep and grow" for "continue"; Rose/taxes compared against a Fritts grocery-tax quote that is not in the batch (WKRN only ever published a Fritts statement, never a direct quotation).\n\nThird non-differentiating-goal medium RESOLVED by user decision 2026-08-02: Rose/school-vouchers d29d9032 ("The overwhelming majority of Tennesseans want parents to have options") is a popularity claim, not Rose''s own commitment -- WVLT records only that he added "the question is how to facilitate those options", so his approach was never printed as a direct quote. Rose is treated as ABSENT on school vouchers. Row kept as a draft with a "NOT FOR LIVE SELECTION" editor_note so a later session does not select it. Replace only with a quote stating what he would do; the NewsChannel5 "Inside Politics" episode is the likeliest source (see ingest-candidates.json).\n\nRankable after fixes: ALL 5 topics have >=2 candidates -- deportation (Blackburn+Fritts), housing (Blackburn+Rose), public-safety-approach (Fritts+Rose), school-vouchers (Blackburn+Fritts, two-way after Rose is pulled), taxes (Blackburn+Rose). 10 of 11 rows are selectable; d29d9032 is intentionally held back.\nAll 11 rows remain readrank_selected=false at the time of this note. NEXT: select one live quote per (candidate, topic) in /admin/readrank-quotes for those 10, then select essentials.refresh_readrank_pipeline_counters(); and confirm rankable_topics = 5.\nPROCESS NOTE: the 2026-08-01 audit passed while two quotes were not in their cited source. audit-quotes has no check that re-fetches source_url and confirms the quote string appears there, nor one that detects a nested quotation (candidate quoting voters) -- both are the failure modes the current checks cannot catch. Fix filed 2026-08-02.'
WHERE id = '2ba201ed-330a-4014-bb5c-b3a2792e26d0';
